{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <iomanip>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nint getGCD(int a, int b) {\n    int candidate = (a > b) ? a : b;\n    while (true) {\n        if (a % candidate == 0 && b % candidate == 0) break;\n        --candidate;\n    }\n    return candidate;\n}\n\ndouble computeError(double x, double y, double p, double q, double& num, double& den) {\n    num = fabs(x * q - y * p);\n    den = y * q;\n    return num / den;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    double x, y, n;\n    double minError = 1e15;\n    int bestNum = 0, bestDen = 1;\n\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n\n    if (n > y) {\n        int g = getGCD((int)x, (int)y);\n        if (g != 1) {\n            x /= g;\n            y /= g;\n        }\n        cout << (int)x << \"/\" << (int)y << endl;\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    for (int b = (int)n; b >= 1; --b) {\n        double a_val = (x * b) / y;\n        if (a_val == floor(a_val)) {\n            bestNum = (int)a_val;\n            bestDen = b;\n            break;\n        } else {\n            double num1, den1;\n            double err1 = computeError(x, y, floor(a_val), b, num1, den1);\n            if (err1 < minError || (fabs(err1 - minError) < 1e-12 && (int)floor(a_val) < bestNum)) {\n                bestNum = (int)floor(a_val);\n                bestDen = b;\n                minError = err1;\n            }\n\n            double num2, den2;\n            double err2 = computeError(x, y, ceil(a_val), b, num2, den2);\n            if (err2 < minError || (fabs(err2 - minError) < 1e-12 && (int)ceil(a_val) < bestNum)) {\n                bestNum = (int)ceil(a_val);\n                bestDen = b;\n                minError = err2;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    int g = getGCD(bestNum, bestDen);\n    if (g != 1) {\n        bestNum /= g;\n        bestDen /= g;\n    }\n\n    cout << bestNum << \"/\" << bestDen << endl;\n\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static int getGCD(int a, int b) {\n        int candidate = (a > b) ? a : b;\n        while (true) {\n            if (a % candidate == 0 && b % candidate == 0) break;\n            --candidate;\n        }\n        return candidate;\n    }\n\n    public static double computeError(double x, double y, double p, double q, double[] result) {\n        double num = Math.abs(x * q - y * p);\n        double den = y * q;\n        result[0] = num;\n        result[1] = den;\n        return num / den;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        double x = scanner.nextDouble();\n        double y = scanner.nextDouble();\n        double n = scanner.nextDouble();\n\n        double minError = 1e15;\n        int bestNum = 0;\n        int bestDen = 1;\n\n        if (n > y) {\n            int g = getGCD((int)x, (int)y);\n            if (g != 1) {\n                x /= g;\n                y /= g;\n            }\n            System.out.println((int)x + \"/\" + (int)y);\n            return;\n        }\n\n        for (int b = (int)n; b >= 1; --b) {\n            double a_val = (x * b) / y;\n            if (a_val == Math.floor(a_val)) {\n                bestNum = (int)a_val;\n                bestDen = b;\n                break;\n            } else {\n                double[] result1 = new double[2];\n                double err1 = computeError(x, y, Math.floor(a_val), b, result1);\n                if (err1 < minError || (Math.abs(err1 - minError) < 1e-12 && (int)Math.floor(a_val) < bestNum)) {\n                    bestNum = (int)Math.floor(a_val);\n                    bestDen = b;\n                    minError = err1;\n                }\n\n                double[] result2 = new double[2];\n                double err2 = computeError(x, y, Math.ceil(a_val), b, result2);\n                if (err2 < minError || (Math.abs(err2 - minError) < 1e-12 && (int)Math.ceil(a_val) < bestNum)) {\n                    bestNum = (int)Math.ceil(a_val);\n                    bestDen = b;\n                    minError = err2;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        int g = getGCD(bestNum, bestDen);\n        if (g != 1) {\n            bestNum /= g;\n            bestDen /= g;\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(bestNum + \"/\" + bestDen);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00013219437096267939, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.001790707348845899, -1.1205610462639015e-05, -0.0003277718205936253, -0.55512535572052, -4.136476854910143e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.47952248173533e-05, -0.0009117737063206732, -0.00026174934464506805, -0.1328473538160324, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.0031802100129425526, -2.8729025871143676e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.099436753473128e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00044312194222584367, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.823885577323381e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.218645588276558